#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:6
msgid "Why and What, not How and Where"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:8
msgid "Avoid documenting irrelevant details that may frequently change."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:11
msgid "// Copyright 2025 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:12
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:13
msgid ""
"// bad\n"
"/// Saves a `User` record to the Postgres database.  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// This function opens a new connection and begins a transaction. It "
"checks  \n"
"/// if a user with the given ID exists with a `SELECT` query. If a user "
"is  \n"
"/// not found, performs an `INSERT`.  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// # Errors  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// Returns an error if any database operation fails.  \n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:25
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:36
msgid "// ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:27
msgid ""
"// good\n"
"/// Atomically saves a user record.  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// # Errors  \n"
"///  \n"
"/// Returns a `db::Error::DuplicateUsername` error if the user (keyed by  \n"
"/// `user.username` field) already exists.  \n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:42
msgid ""
"Motivation: Users want to know the contract of the API (what is guaranteed "
"about this function), rather than implementation details."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:45
msgid ""
"Motivation: Doc comments that explain implementation details become outdated "
"faster than comments that explain the contract."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:48
msgid ""
"Internal information is likely irrelevant to a user. Imagine explaining in a "
"doc comment for a function that you're using `for` loops to solve a problem, "
"what is the point of this information?"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:52
msgid ""
"It could be that the implementation is necessary to explain, but this is "
"likely due to whatever effects or invariants the user of that API needs to "
"be aware of instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:56
msgid ""
"Focus on those effects and invariants instead of the implementation details "
"themselves."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:59
msgid ""
"Reiterate: Implementation details can and will change, so do not explain "
"these details."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/what-why-not-how-where.md:62
msgid ""
"Don't talk about where something is used, this is another instance where "
"this information can become stale quickly."
msgstr ""
